#: templates/admin/privacy.php:21
msgid "What personal data we collect and why we collect it"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:22
msgid "<strong>We have no access to any of the data collected by the plugin.</strong> It is stored in your own database and is never sent to us. The points below are provided so you can describe it in your own privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:23
msgid "Recipe ratings"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:24
msgid "When user ratings are enabled, submitting a rating stores the rating value, the ID of the recipe, the date, and the IP address of the visitor who submitted it. Logged-in visitors also have their user ID stored. If the rating was submitted together with a review, the name, email address and review text supplied in the rating form are stored as well."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:26
msgid "The IP address is stored so that the same visitor cannot rate the same recipe more than once, and to limit how many ratings a single address may submit. It is held only in your own database and is not shared with us or any third party."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:27
msgid "Cookies"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:28
msgid "When a visitor rates a recipe we store a <em>wpzoom-user-rating-recipe-%recipe_ID%</em> cookie (where %recipe_ID% is the ID of the recipe) holding the rating that visitor gave. It lets us show them their own rating when they return, and is one of the measures used to prevent rating spam."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:29
msgid "How long we retain your data"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/privacy.php:30
msgid "The <em>wpzoom-user-rating-recipe-%recipe_ID%</em> cookie is stored for 30 days. Ratings, reviews and their associated IP addresses are stored in your local database indefinitely, until deleted from the Ratings screen or through the Reset Ratings action in the plugin settings."
msgstr ""

